  "label": {
    "en": [
      "A vintage postcard with Russian Cyrillic text, featuring a double-headed eagle emblem (the coat of arms of the Russian Empire) in the top left corner. There is a blue postage stamp in the top right, several postal marks/stamps, and handwritten address lines. The card is labeled 'ПОЧТОВАЯ КАРТОЧКА.' at the top, and contains lines for writing the recipient's address."
    ]
